docs/helm-chart.md

# Node deps for the browser-driven e2e (test/e2e/ui-smoke.js and
# test/e2e/sso-login-page.js tell you to `npm i playwright-core` at the root).
node_modules/

# The cluster name test/gcp/provision.sh leaves for test/gcp/teardown.sh. It is
# written to the working directory and names a real, billing cluster; it belongs
# to one run on one machine and must never be committed.
.gcp-experiment-cluster

# The shared shell libraries the cloud experiment runners source. They are NOT
# a Python distribution artifact, but the stock "Distribution" block above
# ignores `lib/` unanchored, which matches at any depth: without this negation
# test/gcp/lib/ is silently excluded, the three runners are committed WITHOUT
# the code they source, and every one of them breaks on a fresh checkout while
# still passing locally where the files are present. `git add` reports nothing
# and the omission is invisible until someone else clones.
!test/gcp/lib/
!test/gcp/lib/*.sh

# Raw series, verdicts and reports from one cloud experiment run. These are
# timings from a real billing cluster on one machine at one moment: they belong
# to that run, not to the repository. test/gcp/lib/experiment.sh writes them.
test/gcp/runs/

# Soak battery evidence (test/soak). Every run writes a timestamped directory of
# samples, violations and logs here; none of it belongs in the repository.
.soak/
